---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Mustafa Hasnain">
  <section class="page hero">
    <h1>Mustafa Hasnain</h1>
    <p class="subhead">
      I like understanding how networks and systems actually work — then proving it by building the thing myself.
    </p>

    <div class="story">
      <p>
        I'm a Computer Information Systems and Technology student at UT Dallas, and most of what I know about
        networking and infrastructure I've learned by building it rather than reading about it.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's led to a home lab running Active Directory across four virtual machines — a domain controller, a
        routing server, a file server, and a client — plus a Raspberry Pi that watches over all of it, catching
        outages and confirming recoveries in real time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Right now I'm studying for the CompTIA Network+ certification and looking to start my career in IT and
        networking. The projects and qualifications pages have the specifics.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="/projects">See the projects <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      <a href="/qualifications">Qualifications <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
    text-align: center;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .subhead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
  }

  .story {
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: left;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .story p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .cta-row {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .cta-row a {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
</style>
